"answer": "Project Zenith is a high-priority initiative aimed at driving innovation, leveraging cutting-edge technologies, and enhancing core operations, with a total approved budget of $2 million. The project timeline includes a kick-off on June 15th with a $500,000 budget for phase one, led by Sarah Tan. A call for ideas was issued in July, focusing on AI-enhanced data visualization, with proposals due by July 20th. The project has achieved several milestones, including the successful completion of the testing phase (celebrated on October 10th), the design phase, and the testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule. The next phases involve development (led by Omar Jensen), user interface enhancements starting in October, and a focus on predictive analytics. A detailed report on phase two progress will be presented on November 20th, and feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November. Additionally, the team is exploring partnership opportunities with TechInnovate for AI technology."
